---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout page={pages.privacy}>
  <h2>Tool input stays in the browser</h2>
  <p>
    Core formatting, comparison, conversion, inspection, and generation
    operations run in your browser. The application does not send editor text,
    local file contents, token values, clipboard contents, or generated output
    to an application server. Input is not placed in the page URL, logged to the
    production console, or saved in a payload history.
  </p>
  <p>
    Local file controls read files you select into the current tab. Download
    controls create files on your device. Copy controls write the selected
    result to your system clipboard only when you request it. Browser
    extensions, shared devices, and clipboard history operate outside this
    site’s control.
  </p>
  <h2>Ordinary website requests</h2>
  <p>
    Loading a website still makes ordinary network requests for pages, scripts,
    styles, and fonts. Hosting providers may process connection information such
    as IP address, requested path, browser headers, and access timestamps for
    delivery, security, and operational logs. Core transformations do not attach
    your tool input to those requests.
  </p>
  <h2>Preferences and storage</h2>
  <p>
    The theme preference is stored in this browser’s local storage under a
    site-specific preference key. You can remove it through browser site-data
    settings. Tool payloads are kept in tab memory while you use the tool;
    reloading or leaving the page clears this application state. Your browser
    may independently retain form or clipboard history.
  </p>
  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The default version has analytics and advertising disabled and makes no
    requests to analytics or advertising providers. If the operator enables such
    services later, this policy must be updated to identify the providers,
    purposes, data, retention practices, and applicable user choices.
    Third-party scripts may receive ordinary browsing information. Editor input
    and token values must never be attached to analytics events.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where required, advertising must be integrated with an appropriate consent
    management platform before third-party ad requests begin. A generic cookie
    notice alone does not establish legal compliance. Consent and privacy
    requirements depend on the services used and visitors’ jurisdictions.
  </p>
  <h2>Links and communication</h2>
  <p>
    Documentation links lead to third-party sites governed by their own privacy
    policies. URL inspection never fetches or navigates to the pasted
    destination. If you use an email contact link, the message is handled by
    your email provider and the recipient’s email service. The local
    feedback-draft form does not submit a message to this website.
  </p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Use demonstration or sanitized data, avoid production secrets, clear the
    editors when finished, and remove downloaded files or clipboard history if
    necessary. For privacy questions, consult the{' '}
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Operator contact details and
    jurisdiction-specific rights should be reviewed before a public launch.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
